From d663d05b15cc3f5ca2cc827e245bc684a0b6b439 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:57:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: the measured level 5 decision is of one value of
 the offsets, proportional and by picture across a band

The decision of 01935ee was too eager: three measured pictures with one
block above the black level in the outer half of a band left the
offsets aside for the whole video, so that 16:9 opening logos under the
film's offsets, subtitles burnt into a band or a noisy band threw away
a right level 5 block for the rest of the film.

Now (dvbridge_l5check.h):
- a band is contradicted by picture across it, not by something in it:
  more than half of its rows (columns, for the side bands) have blocks
  above the black level in at least 12 of the 16 bands of columns of
  the measurement (6 of 8 bands of rows). A picture that the band cuts
  fills the width; a logo or a line of subtitles does not, nor a few
  bright rows at its edge (dvbridge_l5_band_contradicted(), from the
  raw rows and columns of dvbridge_measure.c; dvbridge_dv_l5_contradicted()
  and its bounding box are gone);
- the decision is of one value of the offsets: a picture with other
  offsets starts a count of its own (dvbridge_l5check_value()), and the
  decision of the value before ends with it: the serializer leaves aside
  only the offsets that were decided on (dvbridge_dv_ignore_l5_of() takes
  them; NULL takes them again), and the window gives them back;
- it is proportional: at least 10 pictures measured with the value (the
  opening, one a second), at least 3 contradicting, 2 s apart or more,
  and more than half of the measured ones. Measuring goes on at the low
  rate, and the offsets are taken again when the contradicting pictures
  are half or fewer.
A level 5 block that fits no reading is now left aside for its value
too, not for the video.

Tested on the host with real pictures of the FEL test stream on zink
over lavapipe (l5gpu_test.c of the front): a letterboxed film after a
dark opening, five 16:9 opening pictures under the film's offsets, a
line of subtitles burnt into the bottom band, three bright rows at the
edge of a band: never left aside; the stream as it is (picture across
its bands) and offsets of 600 rows over bars of 275: left aside at the
tenth measured picture; twelve open matte pictures then the
letterboxed film under the same offsets: left aside, then taken again;
another value: the decision ends. Mutations that each make it fail:
deciding at the first measured picture, without the proportion, and
any content in a band contradicting. 11.8 ms of lavapipe a measured 4K
picture, 609 of 172800 pictures measured in a simulated two hours.
l5_test.c: the decision by value (a fitting value of the same video is
taken), and against 1.0 RC6 the wrong offsets still fail.

kodi.log: "... the level 5 offsets of this video (l r t b) make bars of
... and N of the M pictures measured with them have picture across a
band (...; in the last one, rows or columns of the picture in each
band: ...): they are left aside while they come", "... are taken again:
N of the M pictures ... half or fewer", and "... the level 5 offsets of
this video changed (...): the ones left aside are no longer ...".
